  "timeline": [
    {
      "key": "01_hook",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.79,
      "narration": "What if the Big Bang was the inside of a black hole?"
    },
    {
      "key": "02_hypothesis",
      "start": 4.79,
      "end": 13.35,
      "narration": "Not a fact. Not a discovery. A breathtaking hypothesis called black hole cosmology."
    },
    {
      "key": "03_bounce",
      "start": 13.35,
      "end": 25.15,
      "narration": "In some models, collapse does not end at a singularity. Some quantum gravity ideas replace it with a bounce, opening a new region of expanding space time."
    },
    {
      "key": "04_inside",
      "start": 25.15,
      "end": 34.43,
      "narration": "From inside, that bounce could look like a Big Bang: no center, just space expanding everywhere at once."
    },
    {
      "key": "05_limit",
      "start": 34.43,
      "end": 46.15,
      "narration": "But this is where honesty matters. Our best theories clash in these extreme conditions, and no observation shows our universe was born this way."
    },
    {
      "key": "06_fingerprint",
      "start": 46.15,
      "end": 59.1,
      "narration": "To become science, the idea needs a fingerprint: a unique pattern in the cosmic microwave background, or primordial gravitational waves that rival explanations cannot copy."
    },
    {
      "key": "07_honesty",
      "start": 59.1,
      "end": 65.3,
      "narration": "Until then, the answer is not yes. It is: we do not know."
    },
    {
      "key": "08_cta",
      "start": 65.3,
      "end": 78.1,
      "narration": "That is still astonishing. The cosmos may be stranger than our best story. Universe Impact. Follow for wonder, evidence first."
    }
  ],
